<title>USA: EPA says largest US refinery breaks benzene limits.</title>
<headline>EPA says largest US refinery breaks benzene limits.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The largest oil refinery in the United States, Amoco Corp's plant near Houston, has been violating U.S. emissions on cancer-causing benzene for over a year, according to the U.S. Environmental Protection Agency (EPA).</p>
<p>&quot;There are some benzene emission problems at the Amoco refinery,&quot; said David Bary, a spokesman at EPA's southern regional office in Dallas. &quot;There's no imminent threat, but they're in violation of the Clean Air Act,&quot; he added.</p>
</text>
